# This app needs almost no configuration.
#
# On Render, DATABASE_URL is provided automatically by the blueprint — you do
# NOT need to set it yourself. This file is only useful if you ever run the
# backend on your own machine.
#
# Leave DATABASE_URL unset locally to use a throwaway SQLite file instead of Postgres.

# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dbname

# ---- HERE routing (required for baking geometry) ----------------------------
# HERE_API_KEY=...

# ---- Admin protection ------------------------------------------------------
# While ADMIN_TOKEN is unset, _check_admin() is a no-op and EVERY admin endpoint is
# open — including the ones that spend HERE calls per click and the Config save that
# rewrites every payload and cycle time.
#
# ⚠️ THE VALUE IS THE OUTPUT OF THE COMMAND, NOT THE COMMAND. On 2026-09-09 the live
# deployment was found with ADMIN_TOKEN set to the literal text "openssl rand -hex 24"
# because this comment read as if that were the value. It is not. Run it:
#
#     openssl rand -hex 24        (macOS / Linux / Git Bash)
#
# and paste the 48-character hex string it PRINTS — something like 3f9a1c... — here
# and into the admin token field on the Routes page. Never paste the command itself.
# ADMIN_TOKEN=

# ---- Google Street View (Phase 2.5a, optional) ------------------------------
# Street View imagery in location popups. Entirely optional: with no key set, the
# popups simply show no photo and nothing else changes.
#
# This is Google Maps Platform — a SEPARATE product, key and bill from HERE. Enable
# only the "Street View Static API" for this key and restrict it to your server's IP.
# The key is held by the backend and never sent to the browser.
#
# Cost: metadata lookups are free and consume no quota; IMAGES are billable. The app
# always checks metadata first and never requests an image for a location Google has
# no imagery for. Read the current rate off Google's pricing page — it has changed
# twice recently, so no figure is quoted anywhere in this repo.
# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Optional but recommended: Google's URL signing secret. With it set, requests are
# signed so a leaked key cannot be used elsewhere. Without it, everything still works.
# GOOGLE_MAPS_URL_SIGNING_SECRET=

# ---- Tark Tee road restrictions (Phase 2.5a) --------------------------------
# No key needed. Estonian Transport Administration open data, fetched server-side
# from tarktee.ee and cached for 30 minutes. Nothing to configure.

# The Mapbox token lives in map/config.js (it is a browser token), not here.

# ---- 2026-09-02, Task F: access codes (checked by the server) -----------------
# Set any of these and the three demo codes (submitter123 / planner123 / admin123)
# stop working. An IPT code sees only forecast lines whose `ipt` is that IPT and
# cannot approve. PLANNER_CODE sees every IPT and approves. ADMIN_CODE is planner
# plus the admin surface, which STILL needs ADMIN_TOKEN for /api/admin/*.
# IPT1_CODE=
# IPT2_CODE=
# IPT3_CODE=
# IPT4_CODE=
# IPT5_CODE=
# IPT6_CODE=
# PLANNER_CODE=
# ADMIN_CODE=

# ---- 2026-09-14: the /map/ password and the /help/ staff gate -----------------
# Until today /map/ and /help/ were open to anyone with the URL. They are now gated,
# and with DIFFERENT keys, because they have different audiences.
#
#   /map/    a SHARED PASSWORD (below). Give the string to a stakeholder or the client
#            and they see the corridor without an account.
#   /help/   the STAFF SIGN-IN only. Nothing to configure — it follows the access codes.
#
# ⚠️ THIS FAILS CLOSED, UNLIKE ADMIN_TOKEN. With MAP_PASSWORD unset, an outside visitor
# to /map/ is REFUSED and told the map is not configured. Your own team is unaffected:
# a valid access code, or the cookie a staff sign-in sets, opens the map whether or not
# a password exists. A forgotten MAP_PASSWORD costs you external viewers, never staff.
#
# ⚠️ ROTATING THIS SIGNS EVERYONE OUT. The cookie is signed with a key derived from the
# password, so changing it invalidates every cookie already issued. That is the feature:
# it is how you take access away from someone who should no longer have it.
# MAP_PASSWORD=

# Optional. Set an explicit signing key and the cookie survives a password rotation —
# useful if you rotate the password often and do NOT want to sign everyone out.
# Leave unset and the key is derived from MAP_PASSWORD + ADMIN_TOKEN.
# GATE_SECRET=

# Local development only. MAP_GATE=off reopens BOTH /map/ and /help/ with no password.
# Anything other than off / 0 / false / no leaves the gate ON, including leaving it unset.
# MAP_GATE=off
